he issue: it states that each colony was opened once at the spring inspection, that a colony contributes exactly one row, that the design-by-outcome table counts colonies rather than visits, and that the row count equals the number of independent units; the selected-result line itself asserts 24 independent colonies with one row per colony.\",\"The report's numbers are reproducible from the frozen data: notched arm has 9 survived and 3 died, open arm has 3 survived and 9 died, matching the 2x2 table [[9, 3], [3, 9]], and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value for that table is 0.0391 as reported, so the demonstration of one-row-per-unit is backed by counts that match the data.\",\"The workflow enforces the declaration at load time: load_colonies raises if any colony_id appears on more than one row, so a duplicated independent unit could not have reached the row-independent procedure.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so the lock-follows-declaration question is answered exactly not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["The declared independent-unit column colony_id is consistent with the frozen data: all 24 colony_id values (HV-01 through HV-24) are unique, so each row is one independent unit, and each colony appears in exactly one procedure arm (12 notched, 12 open), so no unit is repeated within or across arms of the Fisher's exact test.","The selected report demonstrates the absence of the issue: it states that each colony was opened once at the spring inspection, that a colony contributes exactly one row, that the design-by-outcome table counts colonies rather than visits, and that the row count equals the number of independent units; the selected-result line itself asserts 24 independent colonies with one row per colony.","The report's numbers are reproducible from the frozen data: notched arm has 9 survived and 3 died, open arm has 3 survived and 9 died, matching the 2x2 table [[9, 3], [3, 9]], and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value for that table is 0.0391 as reported, so the demonstration of one-row-per-unit is backed by counts that match the data.","The workflow enforces the declaration at load time: load_colonies raises if any colony_id appears on more than one row, so a duplicated independent unit could not have reached the row-independent procedure.","No authority lock was minted, so the lock-follows-declaration question is answered exactly not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":6122,"ttft_stream_ms":1810,"time_to_request_ms":25,"type":"result","duration_ms":11893,"uuid":"bf93f305-51f9-46e7-ac26-ddd827454c1f"}
